cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite or reuse these slides, please cite them as below. Individual
  talks carry their own event and date on the deck's cover slide — cite those
  when referring to one talk rather than to the collection.
title: Slides — Frédérick Madore
abstract: >-
  Conference talks, lectures and keynotes on Islam in West Africa, digital
  humanities and artificial intelligence, published as offline-capable
  reveal.js decks on a shared "Broadsheet" theme. Includes the reusable deck
  engine and the build, audit and validation tooling behind the site.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Madore
    given-names: Frédérick
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0959-2092
    affiliation: Africa Multiple Cluster of Excellence, University of Bayreuth
repository-code: https://github.com/fmadore/slides
url: https://slides.frederickmadore.com/
# Mixed on purpose, and narrower than it looks: MIT covers the engine and the
# tooling, CC BY 4.0 the slide text and original figures. Vendored software,
# fonts, institutional logos and externally sourced images are excluded from
# both — see LICENSE.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Islam in West Africa
  - African studies
  - digital humanities
  - artificial intelligence
  - conference presentations
  - reveal.js
